-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What the MIT licence above does not cover
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT licence covers Sierra-III's own code, scripts and documents. These
files are not ours to license, or not under these terms:

1. psp/xmb/campaign/PIC1.PNG, the campaign's XMB wallpaper, is made with
   stills of Halo: Combat Evolved gameplay. It is used under Microsoft's
   Game Content Usage Rules (https://www.xbox.com/en-US/developers/rules)
   and is not under the MIT licence: it may be shared only as those rules
   allow (not for commercial use). Halo: Combat Evolved (c) Microsoft
   Corporation. Sierra-III is not endorsed by or affiliated with Microsoft.

2. The project's own look is not under the MIT licence: the Sierra mark
   (psp/xmb/sierra_mark.svg) and the XMB art made from it or for the
   project (psp/xmb/campaign/ICON0.PNG, psp/xmb/mp/*.PNG). Copyright (c)
   2026 The Sierra-III authors, all rights reserved: they may be shared only
   as part of unmodified copies of Sierra-III. A fork picks its own look.

3. Our patches to GPL programs keep those programs' licences:
   - upstream/invader/*.patch, changes to Invader: GNU GPL version 3
     (Invader's licence);
   - tools/ppsspp_local_patches.diff, changes to PPSSPP: GNU GPL version 2
     or later (PPSSPP's licence).

4. Third-party files carried as they are, each under its own licence:
   - psp/xmb/fonts/Audiowide-Regular.ttf: the Audiowide font by Astigmatic,
     SIL Open Font License 1.1 (psp/xmb/fonts/OFL.txt);
   - psp/include/GLES2/, psp/include/GLES3/, psp/include/KHR/: the Khronos
     Group's OpenGL ES and KHR headers, under the MIT or Apache 2.0 licence
     each names in its header;
   - bake/bundle/licenses/: the Rust standard library's licence texts, as
     the Rust project publishes them.

The engine this port builds on (ChupathingyCE, CC0 1.0) is not in this
repository: the build fetches it at the commit upstream/pins.env pins, and
psp_fixups.py changes a copy of it. UPSTREAM.md lists every upstream, its pin
and its licence. A built release carries the notices of the libraries linked
into it (PSP/GAME/halo/licenses/), and each bake bundle carries LICENSES/ for
the programs inside it.
